### Works with the IntelliJ HTTP client and the VS Code "REST Client" extension.
@base = http://localhost:8080
@actor = registrar.jane

### Reference data
GET {{base}}/api/academic-years

###
GET {{base}}/api/grade-levels

###
GET {{base}}/api/offerings

### Register an application
POST {{base}}/api/applications
Content-Type: application/json
X-Actor: {{actor}}

{
  "applicant": { "firstName": "Ada", "lastName": "Okafor", "dateOfBirth": "2020-03-10" },
  "guardian": { "fullName": "Ngozi Okafor", "email": "ngozi@example.com", "phone": "+2348012345678" },
  "academicYearId": 1,
  "gradeLevelId": 1,
  "documents": [
    { "type": "BIRTH_CERTIFICATE", "nameOnDocument": "Ada Okafor", "dateOnDocument": "2020-03-10" },
    { "type": "IMMUNISATION_RECORD" },
    { "type": "PASSPORT_PHOTO" }
  ]
}

### Run the eligibility rules
POST {{base}}/api/applications/1/eligibility-check
X-Actor: {{actor}}

### Advisory document review (never changes the application)
GET {{base}}/api/applications/1/document-review

### Admit / waitlist / reject
POST {{base}}/api/applications/1/decision
Content-Type: application/json
X-Actor: {{actor}}

{ "decision": "ADMITTED", "reason": "Meets all criteria" }

### History
GET {{base}}/api/applications/1/audit

###
GET {{base}}/api/applications/1/decisions

### Search
GET {{base}}/api/applications?status=ADMITTED&gradeLevelId=1&page=0&size=20

### Add a late document (resets eligibility to PENDING)
POST {{base}}/api/applications/1/documents
Content-Type: application/json
X-Actor: {{actor}}

{ "type": "IMMUNISATION_RECORD" }

### Withdraw
POST {{base}}/api/applications/1/withdraw
X-Actor: {{actor}}
